Came across this issue recently. Metadata was being streamed to the body tag, but there was no need for it, as all the required data is present at build time. We are using: 

`export const dynamic = 'force-static';`

This helped us to get the metadata resolved at build time again, and back inside the Head tag. _All the data we require to generate metadata is available at build time_. Usage example along with `generateMetadata()`:

```
// src/app/[lang]/page.tsx

export const dynamic = 'force-static';

export const generateMetadata = async ({
  params,
}: {
  params: Promise<{ lang: LanguageProperties['code'] }>;
}) => {
  const { lang } = await params;

  const res = await getSingleTranslation(lang, HomePageKeys.metaDescription);

  const fallbackDescription = res
    ? res.text
    : '';

  return await getMetadataForRoute({
    lang,
    pathname: '/',
    title: undefined,
    description: fallbackDescription,
  });
};
```

We added it once to the base or home page file, and seems to be resolving all the routes on the same app router path the same way. No need to make any tweaks in next.config.ts

As far as I know, this is currently a limitation of Lightning CSS which is used in the background to parse and transform CSS. https://github.com/parcel-bundler/lightningcss/issues/6

Judging by that issue I've linked, this isn't going to be updated and Lightning CSS won't support this `:global {}` type of selector where you can nest other selectors under it. Your best bet is to rewrite this CSS.

If for example you've used `:global {}` like this:

```css
:global {
  .icon {
    ...
  }

  .test {
    ...
  }
}
```

You must rewrite it to use the function like syntax:

```css
:global(.icon) {
  ...
}

:global(.test) {
  ...
}
```

@ALWISHARIFF because you mentioned me on my issue I took a quick look at this and Roboto just isn't being used in your next 14 example. That is Times New Roman.

In Next 14 next doesn't appear to load the fonts with the font family set as the actual name of the font, it adds a suffix to it requiring you to use the provided helpers to fetch that name or to fetch the style needed.

If you want to use the font like in your next 14 example just set Times New Roman instead of Roboto.

