I've found that the OpenTelemetry nodejs auto instrumentations (HTTP being the relevant for this issue) must be run _before_ Next.js itself starts up. This is because the server will start before the `http` module is monkey patched. Which means you'd have to use the `node --register` method (but this causes other issues, such as `.env` not being loaded because that happens as part of the server start)

Alternatively, if you do a top-level registration in `instrumentation.ts` outside of the `register` function, it will cause the instrumentations to run _before_ the server executes. When this happens, the server is monkey patched first and then Next.js will call to create a server which is now instrumented. With that, the `http.server.request.duration` metric will be emitted by the HTTP instrumentation.

