My understanding is that Next 16 treats generateMetadata as a dynamic segment. Please correct me if I'm wrong about any of this, but this is the behavior I've observed. 

If `generateMetadata` relies on retrieved data (even if it's the same data as the Page content) Next will make a separate RSC request for it. Because these are separate requests to the server, memoized functions like `fetch` or React `cache` do not work because those only deduplicate within the _same_ request.

Using `"use cache"` in your data retrieval function will prevent additional retrievals on subsequent page loads/prefetches, but it is not a solution for the initial page load/prefetch because the page + metadata requests happen in such close proximity that there is no time for the cache object to be created, and the data fetch ends up happening twice no matter what.

Compared to previous versions this means Next 16 _at a minimum_ doubles the number of requests/DB lookups compared to previous versions when using the same data for page content and metadata. In my case we're using GraphQL to retrieve data from a separate backend app, and the doubling of requests impacts resources in both apps.

Here's an example of a Page.tsx from my app, using Cache Components, which results in duplicate GraphQL requests:

```typescript
async function getData(params: PageParams)  {
  "use cache";
  cacheTag(
    ...getCacheTags({
      network: params.network,
      site: params.site,
      postType: "page",
      slug: params.slug,
    }),
  );
  cacheLife("weeks");

  try {
    return makeApolloRequest<GetPageQuery>(
      params.network,
      params.site,
      GetPage,
      {
        pageSlug: params.slug,
      },
    )
  } catch (err) {
    notFound();
  }
}

export async function generateMetadata(props: PageProps): Promise<Metadata> {
  const params = await props.params;
  const { data } = await getData(params);
  const canonicalFallback = `${getCanonicalBase(
    params.network,
    params.site,
  )}${params.slug}/`;

  const seo = data?.page?.seo;
  return createMetadata({
    ...seo,
    canonical: seo?.canonical || canonicalFallback,
  });
}

export default async function Page(props: PageProps) {
  const params = await props.params;
  const { data } = await getData(params);

  if (!data?.page) {
    notFound();
  }

  const templateValues = {
    blocksRaw: data?.page?.blocks,
    postTitle: data?.page?.title,
    templateName: data?.page?.template?.templateName ?? "",
  };

  return (
    <PageTemplate {...templateValues} />
  );
}

```

