These are two possible behaviors, and when they happen:
- the ECMAScript standard compliant one (class fields), the output is `PasswordSignInRequest {..., username: undefined}`
  - running it untranspiled in a browser/Node.js
  - Turbopack doesn't rewrite anything here, so behaves the same. Types are merely stripped if they exist
  - Typescript compiler with `useDefineForClassFields: true` (or a `target` of ES2022 or higher)
- the behavior predating standardized class fields, the output is `PasswordSignInRequest {..., username: "jon"}`:
  - Webpack always rewrites this to remove all all the class fields
  - Turbopack with `useDefineForClassFields: false`
  - Typescript compiler with `useDefineForClassFields: false` (or a `target` of ES2021 or older)
  - in this case, transpiling causes the class fields to be removed entirely:
```js
class SignInRequest {
  constructor(data) {
    this.username = data.username
    this._discriminator = 'SignInRequest'
