I am updating the docs, but there are some cases where the `.clear` method works, it is just not part of the `next/headers` cookies, and it is also not part of the `NextResponse` cookies, where you have to delete one by one.

```ts
import { NextRequest, NextResponse } from "next/server";

export async function POST(request: NextRequest) {
  // Read cookies from the request
  const session = request.cookies.get('session');
  const allCookies = request.cookies.getAll();

  // Clear cookies from the request (other request.cookies reads will see empty cookies)
  request.cookies.clear();

  // To actually delete cookies on the client
  const response = NextResponse.json({ success: true });
  response.cookies.delete('session');
  response.cookies.delete('auth-token');

  return response;
}
```

One practical case is making sure that no cookies arrive upstream in middleware/proxy:

```ts
import { NextResponse, type NextRequest } from "next/server";

export default function proxy(req: NextRequest) {
  req.cookies.clear();

  return NextResponse.next({
    request: req,
  });
}
```

