this is what claude code came up with to make `sharp` work in local dev/prod with bun+turbopack:

```ts
import { createRequire } from "node:module";

/**
 * Load sharp, working around a Turbopack + Bun dev server bug.
 *
 * Turbopack externalises native packages by creating hashed symlinks
 * (e.g. `sharp-20c6a5da84e2135f`) in `.next/dev/node_modules/`.
 * Bun's require() cannot resolve these hashed names, so the normal
 * `import("sharp")` that Turbopack rewrites fails at runtime.
 *
 * In development we use createRequire anchored to the project root to
 * resolve sharp directly from the real node_modules. In production the
 * normal require works because vercel externalises sharp correctly.
 *
 * @see https://github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/86866
 * @see https://github.com/oven-sh/bun/issues/25370
 */
let sharp: typeof import("sharp");

if (process.env.NODE_ENV === "development") {
  const req = createRequire(`${process.cwd()}/`);
  sharp = req("sharp");
} else {
  sharp = require("sharp");
}

export default sharp;
```

