I may be missing context here, but I've seen similar view transition failures in RTL documents where the snapshot pseudo-elements don't inherit `direction` from the document root. In some browsers, `::view-transition-old(root)` and `::view-transition-new(root)` default to `direction: ltr`, which can cause layout mismatches or white flashes during the transition.

If you can add this to a global stylesheet, it's worth testing:

```css
::view-transition-old(root),
::view-transition-new(root) {
  direction: inherit;
}
```

This explicitly forces the pseudo-elements to respect the document's `dir="rtl"`. It isn't a guaranteed fix, but it's a small change that often resolves direction-related snapshot oddities without needing to touch the Next.js internals.

