When using `global-not-found.tsx`, the not-found page is rendered **outside of the App Router**.  
Because it does not have router context, client-side navigation (e.g. `next/link`) is unavailable.

You can use the following approach, but it is **not recommended**:

```tsx
export default function GlobalNotFound() {
  return (
    <html>
      <body>
        <p>Not found</p>
        <a href="/">Go home</a>
      </body>
    </html>
  );
}
```
Instead, use the standard App Router not-found page.

`app/not-found.tsx`
```tsx
import Link from 'next/link';

export default function NotFound() {
  return (
    <>
      <p>Not found</p>
      <Link href="/">Go home</Link>
    </>
  );
}
```

Remove `globalNotFound: true` from `next.config.ts.`

If changes do not apply, clear the build cache:

` rm -rf .next `

For most applications, `app/not-found.tsx` is the recommended and simplest solution for creating a custom global not-found page.

