## On the fix shape

The invariant that seems to matter: **a settled action should only advance the queue if it is still the queue head.** The workaround we run in production (patch-package on 16.2.6) replaces the unconditional `runRemainingActions` in (a) the `action.discarded` branch of `handleResult` and (b) the rejection callback with:

```js
if (actionQueue.pending === action) {
  runRemainingActions(actionQueue, setState)
} else if (actionQueue.pending === null && actionQueue.needsRefresh) {
  actionQueue.needsRefresh = false
  actionQueue.dispatch({ type: ACTION_REFRESH }, setState)
}
```

A discarded action is never the head (the navigation replaced it), so the guard is exact, and the intended "discarded revalidating action triggers a refresh once the queue drains" behavior is preserved.

For comparison with the approach in #88550 (skip applying the result when `actionQueue.state !== prevState`): that prevents the stale *commit*, but the stale-seeded action still *starts* while the navigation is in flight — so it captures pre-navigation state and its server-action POST is issued against the pre-navigation `canonicalUrl`, and the discarded branch still advances the queue past the running navigation. Guarding at the queue-head level means queued actions don't start until the navigation settles, so they capture post-navigation state and POST to the correct URL.

Happy to provide more detail or test candidate fixes against our production workload.

