To address the issue of malformed Origin headers in Next.js Server Actions, we need to enhance the `parseOriginHost` function to handle invalid URLs and prevent unhandled exceptions. Here's the improved implementation:
```typescript
function parseOriginHost(originHeader: string): string | undefined {
  if (originHeader === "null") return "null";

  try {
    const url = new URL(originHeader);
    return url.host;
  } catch (error) {
    // Log the error for debugging purposes
    console.error(`Invalid Origin header: ${originHeader}`, error);
    // Return a sentinel value to indicate an invalid origin
    return "\x00INVALID_ORIGIN";
  }
};
```
