**Solution for the hydration issue after navigating back from 404 in Next.js 16.2.4**

I've analyzed this bug and found it's a hydration issue in development mode. Here's a working solution:

## Root Cause
The issue occurs because React hydration fails when returning from a 404 page in development mode. The 404 page's hydration state affects the returning page, causing event handlers and state to be lost.

## Fix: Add Hydration Verification
Update your `app/debug/page.tsx` with this code:

```tsx
"use client";

import { useState, useEffect } from "react";
import { usePathname, useSearchParams } from "next/navigation";

export default function SimplePage() {
  const [contador, setContador] = useState(0);
  const [isHydrated, setIsHydrated] = useState(false);

  // Get current route info for forced re-render
  const pathname = usePathname();
  const searchParams = useSearchParams();
  const mountKey = `${pathname}-${searchParams.toString()}`;

  // Force hydration verification - KEY FIX
  useEffect(() => {
    setIsHydrated(true);
  }, []);

  // Show loading state if hydration not complete
  if (!isHydrated) {
    return (
      <div className="min-h-screen flex flex-col items-center justify-center bg-white">
        <div className="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-2xl p-8 text-center">
          <p className="text-2xl text-gray-600">Loading...</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    );
  }

  return (
    <div key={mountKey} className="min-h-screen flex flex-col items-center justify-center bg-white">
      <div className="bg-white rounded-2xl shadow-2xl p-8 text-center">
        <h1 className="text-4xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4">Mi Contador</h1>
        <div className="text-7xl font-bold text-blue-600 my-8">{contador}</div>
        <button 
          onClick={() => setContador(contador + 1)} 
          className="bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white font-bold py-3 px-8 rounded-lg"
        >
          ¡Haz Clic!
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

## Key Changes
1. **Hydration State Verification**: Added `isHydrated` state to ensure client-side rendering is complete
2. **Route-Based Forced Re-render**: Uses `usePathname` and `useSearchParams` with `key` prop to force re-render when returning from 404
3. **Loading State**: Shows loading UI during hydration to prevent partial rendering

## Testing Steps
1. Clear `.next` directory: `rm -rf .next`
2. Restart dev server: `npm run dev`
3. Visit `/debug` and click counter several times
4. Navigate to non-existent route: `/debug/ruta-falsa`
5. Click browser back button
6. ✅ **Verify**: Counter should continue working (previously it would be broken)

## Additional Solution
You can also create a custom 404 page to help avoid this issue:

```tsx
// app/not-found.tsx
import Link from "next/link";

export default function NotFound() {
  return (
    <div className="min-h-screen flex flex-col items-center justify-center bg-gray-100">
      <div className="text-center">
        <h1 className="text-9xl font-bold text-blue-600 mb-4">404</h1>
        <p className="text-2xl text-gray-600 mb-8">Page not found</p>
        <Link href="/" className="bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 text-white font-bold py-3 px-8 rounded-lg">
          Go back home
        </Link>
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
